>
> Tourists and Archaeologists excel at flexibility ...

This suggests a general learning strategy -  Learn spells from casting
classes like wizard and monk (and priest and so on down the scale
of casting ability).  Learn missile combat from ranged classes like
ranger and rogue (and valk and samurai and so on though the scale
of multifire missile skills).  Learn melee combat from twoweapon
classes like valk and samurai (and so on down the scale of melee
ability).  Learn generalist from archeologist and tourist and so on.
Learn riding from knights and so on.  Learn specialty skills from
specific classes.

Get too specialized in one form, say melee, and you'll end up
rushing face to face and dying as you get deeper.  Get too specialized
in another form, say spells, and you'll end up trapped in alleys
running out of energy.  But learn all of the major general skills
and as your characters get deeper and stronger you'll learn to
use the crossover skills well.

> I'd personally recommend starting as a Valkyrie or a Samurai,

Note that both get expert at specific missiles in addition to being
powerhouse melee characters.  And they can still cast the
occasional spell.



